2026-10-10T01:12:53Z  NOTE      fix: isAuthFailure now takes the HTTP status only and classifies 401/403 as auth failures; the error-message parameter is deleted so the old substring-matching failure shape cannot be written again. Server text, byte counts, clip ids and Qt transfer errorStrings have all been observed to contain 401/Unauthorized with no auth failure present — the old text match tore down live sessions (bearer dropped, NeedsReauth, needsReauth emitted). 403 comes from the board prescription; a captured 403 on an entitlement-gated surface would be worth revisiting, but status-based classification is deterministic where text matching was not.
